	(text "3x LEM HOYS 200-S/SP33 on the motor phase busbars + 300 A window comparator per phase - SPEC.md 8.1, 9.1 / DECISIONS.md D019"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "cada9c93-8a25-4c46-9063-d8102c490e7a")
	)

	(text "LEM HOYS 200-S/SP33 (U501-U503), datasheet 21Oct2021/v6:\n  Pinout (p.15 'Connection'): 1 = UC +3.3 V, 2 = GND, 3 = Uout, 4 = Uref (IN/OUT), 5 = OCD (open drain, active low).\n  Sensitivity 2.3 mV/A, Uref 1.65 V +/-20 mV (internal ref behind Rref 130-300R, overdrivable 0.5-1.7 V), range +/-500 A, BW 180 kHz (p.6).\n  Primary = busbar through aperture: IP+ -> IP- is PHASE_x -> PHASE_x_OUT; Uout > Uref for positive IP in the arrow direction (p.15).\n  Cref 1 uF / CUC 47 nF in the connection figure are INTERNAL to the transducer (p.15) - no external caps required by the DS;\n  100 nF per device fitted anyway as local supply decoupling at the board-side connector [TBV].\n\nUref NOT bused: each Uref pin is a driven output (and an overdrive input, p.6/p.13). Paralleling three would fight the\ninternal references through their 130-300R series resistances -> individual I_REF_1..3 to the MCU ADC (ratiometric use).\n\n300 A hardware trip (SPEC 9.1): 300 A x 2.3 mV/A = 690 mV about 1.65 V -> thresholds 2.34 V / 0.96 V.\nDivider off +3.3 V: 9.53k / 13.7k / 9.53k (E96, 1%) -> 2.3401 V and 0.9600 V nominal (<0.05% from target, ~101 uA string).\nThresholds are absolute: Uref tolerance +/-20 mV shifts the trip by ~ +/-9 A; ratiometric to the same 3.3 V rail as the transducer.\n\nWindow comparator truth table (open-drain: OUT = LOW when V- > V+), all six outputs wire-OR'd on OC_TRIP:\n  A (upper): V+ = 2.34 V, V- = Vout  ->  LOW when Vout > 2.34 V  (I > +300 A)\n  B (lower): V+ = Vout,   V- = 0.96 V ->  LOW when Vout < 0.96 V  (I < -300 A)\n  |I| < 300 A: both outputs Hi-Z -> OC_TRIP held HIGH by R907 4.7k pull-up (supervisor sheet).\n  Trip (either polarity) pulls OC_TRIP LOW -> supervisor U901D (NAND as inverter, pin 13) clocks the 74AUP1G74 fault latch.\n  This restores the original PALTA active-low wired-OR ~OC_Fault structure (D018/D019).\n\nTransducer OCD pins (open drain, active low, threshold 2.92 x Ipn ~ 584 A pk +/-10%, p.6) are also wire-OR'd onto OC_TRIP\nas an independent backup trip; the DS p.15 pull-up 'R' to UC is provided by the shared R907. EEPROM-error forces Uout to\nGND (p.5 note 1) -> caught by the lower comparator. [deviation from task brief: OCD connected, not left NC]\n\nNo comparator hysteresis fitted [TBV]: outputs are wire-OR'd onto a latched line (supervisor latches the first falling\nedge), so chatter cannot un-trip; per-comparator feedback would couple all three phase thresholds through the shared net.\n\nRC anti-alias 100R + 1 nF [TBV] on each I_PH_x (fc ~ 1.6 MHz; transducer Rout 2-5R, CL max 6 nF, p.6).\nComparator part [TBV]: LM2903-class dual open-drain (doc/datasheets/LM2903.pdf); note TI's open-drain dual is TLV7042\n(TLV7032 is push-pull) - keep open-drain for the wired-OR."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175.26 105 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ca4a4e6d-fd1c-4f57-86e1-1d7bb223b03c")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
